Step 1: Create the D1 Database
1.	Go to https://dash.cloudflare.com
2.	In the left sidebar click Workers & Pages
3.	Click D1 (under Storage)
4.	Click Create database
5.	Name it: ts-drive
6.	Click Create
After it’s created you’ll see the database.
Click on it → go to the Settings tab and copy the Database ID (long UUID). Keep it for later if needed.
________________________________________
Step 2: Create the Worker
1.	Still in Workers & Pages, click Create → Create Worker
2.	Give it a name, e.g. ts-collaboration-drive
3.	Click Deploy (this creates an empty “Hello World” worker)
________________________________________
Step 3: Paste the code
1.	After deploy, click Edit code
2.	Delete everything in the editor
3.	Paste the full contents of worker.js
4.	Click Save and Deploy
________________________________________
Step 4: Bind the D1 database
1.	Go back to the Worker’s page
2.	Click the Settings tab
3.	Scroll to Bindings → click Add → choose D1 database
4.	
o	Variable name: DB
o	D1 database: select ts-drive
5.	Click Save
6.	Redeploy if it asks (or just click Deploy again)
________________________________________
Step 5: Test
Open your Worker URL (something like https://ts-collaboration-drive.your-subdomain.workers.dev)
You should see the login page.
